messages[16]{user,text}:
  user_2,[00:00] Hi, is this Rohan Deshmukh? This is Vikram Patel from Omni Insurance Group, calling about your health policy.
  user_1,[00:05] Umm, yes speaking... hi Vikram.
  user_2,[00:10] Great, thanks. I see your policy—Health Plan ID HP-2023-0456—has reached its expiry date as of 30/09/2026.
  user_1,[00:15] Oh... already? I thought it was still active.
  user_2,[00:18] Yeah, the system shows it's marked as Expired. I wanted to discuss renewal options—
  user_1,[00:22] -- sorry, can you repeat that? I was just checking my email.
  user_2,[00:25] Sure, I said your current health policy expired last month. We can either renew the same coverage or look at a new plan.
  user_1,[00:30] Hmm, what's the difference? I don't want any surprise premium hikes.
  user_2,[00:35] Well, the renewal keeps your existing terms, but rates might increase by about 5% due to market adjustments. A new plan could give you broader network access, but the premium could be higher.
  user_1,[00:45] [sighs] I see. Honestly, I was hoping to keep the same plan. Is there any way to lock the current rate?
  user_2,[00:50] We could lock in a 1‑year renewal at the current rate, but it requires payment within the next 7 days. After that, the standard increase applies.
  user_1,[00:55] alright, let me think. Can you send me the renewal details via email?
  user_2,[01:00] Sure thing, I'll email you the quote and the renewal form right after this call.
  user_1,[01:05] Thanks, Vikram. Appreciate the help.
  user_2,[01:10] No problem, Rohan. Feel free to call back if you have any questions. Have a good day!
  user_1,[01:15] You too, bye.